{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-act-20-1","title":"Acts 20:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Paul goes to Macedonia, and thence to Troas. 7 He celebrates the Lord's supper, and preaches. 9 Eutychus having fallen down dead is raised to life. 13 He continues his travels; 17 and at Miletum he calls the elders together, tells them what shall befall to himself, 28 commits God's flock to them, 29 warns them of false teachers, 32 commends them to God, 36 prays with them, and departs.</p>\n<p>after. 19:23-41 embraced. 10,37; 21:5,6; Ge 48:10; 1Sa 20:41,42; Ro 16:16; 1Co 16:20 2Co 13:12; 1Th 5:26 to go. 19:21; 1Co 16:5; 2Co 7:5; 1Ti 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-20-2","title":"Acts 20:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>those. 6; 16:12; 17:1,10 given. 7,11; 2:40; 14:22; 15:41; Col 1:28; 1Th 2:3,11; 4:1 Cir. A.M. 4064. A.D. 60. Greece.That is Greece properly so called, bounded on the west by Epirus, on the east by the Aegean sea, on the north by Macedonia, and on the south by the Peloponnesus. In its largest acceptation it also comprehended all Macedonia, Thessaly, Epirus, Peloponnesus, and the near by islands.</p>\n<p>Zec 9:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-20-3","title":"Acts 20:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the Jews. 19; 9:23,24; 23:12-15; 25:3; Ezr 8:31; Pr 1:11; Jer 5:26; 2Co 7:5 2Co 11:26 sail. 18:18; 21:3; Ga 1:21 he purposed. 19:21; 2Co 1:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-act-20-4","title":"Acts 20:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ACT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Sopater. Ro 16:21 Sosipater. Berea. 17:10-12 Aristarchus. 19:29; 27:2; Col 4:10; Phm 1:24 Gaius. Ro 16:23; 3Jo 1:1 Derbe. 14:6,20; 2Co 8:23,24 Timotheus. 16:1; 